#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564553} :activity/id #uuid "a33f7cdf-c097-51ce-a889-89b173e9d05f" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050726 :topic/id #uuid "61838998-9541-5ba0-829a-1421ece4cbfb" :topic/math-academy-id 3132} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564543 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520509 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b2efb8c-2656-5a9e-bdf4-74177ad5bfa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520055} {:answer/id #uuid "ab956e6c-1981-5cd4-973f-cb9d389db8f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520225} {:answer/id #uuid "ada77caf-e98c-55fb-aefb-f3d728826900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520230} {:answer/id #uuid "dafadf4d-f436-5d63-ba00-63f2baf56d03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520302} {:answer/id #uuid "e183294d-0160-5657-9a79-b2a38d4cd596" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520319}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520302} :answer-field/id #uuid "92ef2ffd-6bce-5a3c-9878-3c95874f4572" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520412}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "eeba80ad-bee9-5269-baef-fbd3bd2d6cda" :question/math-academy-id "q-96323" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $Σ$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the matrices $U$ and $V?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the singular value decomposition of $A$ using the usual algorithm.\n\n- **Step 1.** Compute ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}73 & -24 \\\\ -24 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: From the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=9$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=1.$\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$):\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\sigma }_{1}^{2}=81,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-81I & =[\\begin{aligned}73 & -24 \\\\ -24 & 9\\end{aligned}]-81[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -24 \\\\ -24 & -72\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-81I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\sigma }_{2}^{2}=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-I & =[\\begin{aligned}73 & -24 \\\\ -24 & 9\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}72 & -24 \\\\ -24 & 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$: Since we know the singular values and right singular vectors, we can compute the columns of $U$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute ${u}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{27}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U$ and $V:$\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "0daf925a-435b-5aa2-8acf-a1aac6e83791" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564570}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564553 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496274 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ae24d11-1cd8-53d0-ad47-5b285f4d0b75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495605} {:answer/id #uuid "67a53e3a-1703-5b02-8afb-8f54ac862fec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495739} {:answer/id #uuid "68598054-f8a2-58e6-b3cf-31bcc49b1676" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495742} {:answer/id #uuid "97e9def0-f134-5fa8-8ec0-c84afe6f5876" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495850} {:answer/id #uuid "fadf9222-3d73-5771-87bf-4aacd4a26f7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496062}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495742} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3d56696-4ed6-5583-85eb-387af7ed31be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496201}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "79aa6457-0ad1-5b78-8ab5-2196791a63cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-95906" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A,$ $Σ,$ and $V$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ what is the second column of $U?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ and ${\\sigma }_{i}\\ne 0,$ then the $i$th column of $U$ can be found as\n\n$$\n{u}_{i}=\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{i}}A{v}_{i},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${v}_{i}$ is the $i$th column of the matrix $V.$\n\nFrom the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that the singular values are ${\\sigma }_{1}=9$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=1.$ Therefore, the second column of $U$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "33df4382-d71f-54aa-802f-de21b261aecd" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564594}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564568 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395121 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5dd82220-ad9a-5d23-9059-b9e91a7e8ddf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395123} {:answer/id #uuid "c425653f-089a-5c30-8706-e4cbc10d613d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395124} {:answer/id #uuid "9c91095b-22b2-54a7-b096-79affb1e80fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395125} {:answer/id #uuid "9e80b2f7-83bf-5266-afbf-542740fe0731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395126} {:answer/id #uuid "aeddcf0b-022c-51c6-96fa-c8ec1b75756b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395127}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395126} :answer-field/id #uuid "af024373-62e6-5fa0-a940-575a299d6f21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395122}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4df080fa-5765-5104-a801-ac51915d6839" :question/math-academy-id "q-96318" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 6 \\\\ -9 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}} & \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A,$ $Σ,$ and $V$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ what is the first column of $U?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ and ${\\sigma }_{i}\\ne 0,$ then the $i$th column of $U$ can be found as\n\n$$\n{u}_{i}=\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{i}}A{v}_{i},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${v}_{i}$ is the $i$th column of the matrix $V.$\n\nFrom the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that the singular values are ${\\sigma }_{1}=10$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=7.$ Therefore, the first column of $U$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 6 \\\\ -9 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{40}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "83da4fcb-da5c-5ebd-a4f5-98796e047c6f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564543}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564570 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186418154 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25daf057-15c3-5df1-bf49-09f15c637373" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418096} {:answer/id #uuid "6a0c4372-f45d-517d-808e-21d13a9bf422" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418108} {:answer/id #uuid "8acd0089-c49b-5e7a-844c-82b71ed297ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418120} {:answer/id #uuid "a31a83ba-e84f-5abf-a4d8-18b90f30cc16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418124} {:answer/id #uuid "bcaeadf0-9be9-5ef1-89b2-4becdc0e101d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418127}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186418120} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e6d9098-542a-5974-8eb5-0894237bc643" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418146}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "345be953-89e4-5540-a9e1-d54a38da924f" :question/math-academy-id "q-96358" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $Σ$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the matrices $U$ and $V?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the singular value decomposition of $A$ using the usual algorithm.\n\n- **Step 1.** Compute ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: From the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=3$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=2.$\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$):\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\sigma }_{1}^{2}=9,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-9I & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{bmatrix}-9\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-9I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\sigma }_{2}^{2}=4,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-4I & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{bmatrix}-4\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-4I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A.$: Since we know the singular values and right singular vectors, we can compute the columns of $U$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute ${u}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U$ and $V:$\n\n$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "87122226-7320-5d34-b3e1-309f1140548c"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564594 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371332 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b660dca2-4ca0-5220-9afe-a9076fa7f8e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371334} {:answer/id #uuid "ce67d9df-4bd2-5a78-8e66-b4c709d6c82d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371335} {:answer/id #uuid "dd9aa46a-026e-57a2-82a4-ce39c0ebc8be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371336} {:answer/id #uuid "9c54d3bd-417c-54c8-9f91-a3f0633cad1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371337} {:answer/id #uuid "da61597e-fd43-5b36-b772-f50c15912527" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{13}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371338}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371335} :answer-field/id #uuid "a23b8009-d363-5ace-91d8-9b9ed023f43a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371333}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "01aea047-32df-527d-acda-292ec1b804c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-96248" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}{v}_{11} & {v}_{12} \\\\ {v}_{21} & {v}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ what is the value of $|{v}_{11}|+|{v}_{21}|?$" :question/worked-solution "If $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ the columns of $V$ must be the right singular vectors of $A,$ i.e., the unit eigenvectors of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFrom the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that the singular values are ${\\sigma }_{1}=7$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=3.$ So, the first column of $V$ corresponds to the singular value ${\\sigma }_{1}=7.$\n\nHence, we need to find a unit eigenvector of ${A}^{T}\\,A$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\sigma }_{1}^{2}=49.$ \n\n- Computing ${A}^{T}\\,A,$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}41 & -16 \\\\ -16 & 17\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Computing ${A}^{T}\\,A-49I,$ we get\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}\\,A-49I=\\begin{bmatrix}41 & -16 \\\\ -16 & 17\\end{bmatrix}-49\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & -16 \\\\ -16 & -32\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Seeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-49I)v=0$ gives the eigenvector $v=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Dividing $v$ by its norm, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n|{v}_{11}|+|{v}_{21}|=|-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}|+|\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}|=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "efda492f-25e3-5015-b6b0-eea97e75b0a2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564568}}] :activity/title "Singular Value Decomposition of 2x2 Matrices" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563965}]}
